      "source": [
        "The NIWE 150 m wind-resource dataset contains 19,475,568 spatial observations covering the Indian region. Full-dataset chunk processing was used for data-quality validation and global descriptive statistics, while a representative sample of approximately 390,000 observations was used for visualization and exploratory analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset contains continuous spatial wind-resource variables including mean wind speed, Weibull parameters, air density, and wind power density. Strong positive correlations were observed among wind speed, Weibull scale factor, and wind power density, indicating potential feature redundancy.\n",
        "\n",
        "Statistical outlier analysis identified extreme observations in several variables; these observations were retained because statistical extremeness does not necessarily indicate invalid geographical or meteorological conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "The spatial analysis confirms a predominantly regular coordinate grid and reveals substantial geographical variation in wind-resource characteristics across the study region.\n",
        "\n",
        "These findings provide the foundation for integrating terrain-related variables and subsequently applying PCA, K-Means, and DBSCAN for wind-energy site suitability analysis."
